From: Pedro Baltazar <pedrobtz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Do not clone an option inside selectedcontent into it

maybe_clone_option_into_selectedcontent() runs whenever an option element
is popped while a <selectedcontent> start tag has been seen. In the
automatic state it first destroys selectedcontent's children. When the
option being popped is itself inside selectedcontent, that destroys the
option (and any open element between the two) and then reads it: a
heap use-after-free, reachable from untrusted input such as

  <selectedcontent><option>a<option selected>b

and a dangling pointer on the stack of open elements when an element
between the two is still open.

The standard clones into the selectedcontent of the option's own select;
an option inside that selectedcontent is not one of its options. Return
early when the option is a descendant of the target.

Found by fuzzing zuhtml's copy under AddressSanitizer. To be offered
upstream at https://codeberg.org/gumbo-parser/gumbo-parser.
---
--- a/parser.c
+++ b/parser.c
@@ -1049,6 +1049,15 @@
   if (!selectedcontent) {
     return;
   }
+  // An option inside the selectedcontent element is not an option of the
+  // select it mirrors, and cloning it would first destroy selectedcontent's
+  // children: the option itself, and any open element between the two,
+  // while they are still in use.
+  for (const GumboNode* n = option_node->parent; n; n = n->parent) {
+    if (n == selectedcontent) {
+      return;
+    }
+  }
   if (option_node->type != GUMBO_NODE_ELEMENT && option_node->type != GUMBO_NODE_TEMPLATE) {
     return;
   }
